{
  "_comment": [
    "Catalog parse corpus. Each case is one catalog document.",
    "valid=true: parse succeeds; `messages` is the expected flat result keyed by dotted path. A message is {params, text} or {params, plural}; text is a segment list: {\"t\": literal} or {\"p\": param name}. Adjacent literals are merged; empty literals are omitted.",
    "valid=false: parse fails with exactly `code` at dotted message `key` (\"\" = whole document). Only the first error in document order is pinned; each invalid case contains exactly one fault.",
    "`doc` is the catalog as JSON; `raw` replaces it when the fault is in the bytes (invalid JSON, duplicate object key, trailing data). schema_gap: the fault is not expressible in catalog.schema.json, so the schema accepts the document.",
    "All text is fake."
  ],
